ff.yaml` -> verdict JSON {state: received|accepted|rejected|needs-information, reasons[]}. Hard rejects: any null required identity (archive sha256, bytes, image config id, executable sha256, model manifest sha256, workload sha256, argv), archive hash/bytes mismatch vs recomputed bytes, platform != linux/amd64, mounts not in allowlist {model:ro, workload:ro, results:rw}, any key containing shell/script/host-path execution (`script`, `shell`, `cmd` strings, docker socket, privileged), network_after_staging != none. `accepted` only if all hold. Note: `received`/`accepted`/`rejected`/`needs-information` are RECEIPT states, separate from execution status and test verdict — never emit \"passed\".\n2. cc/engine_handoff/README.md — agent-facing: purpose, inputs/outputs, what it can NOT certify (image contents are not certified beyond the recomputed archive hash and build-record; metadata check is not numerical correctness).\n3. cc/engine_handoff/test_engine_handoff.py (pytest, small fixtures only, no GPU/Docker): happy path -> accepted; null sha -> rejected/needs-information; tampered archive (flip a byte) -> rejected; wrong platform -> rejected; extra mount or privileged key -> rejected.\nDraft handoff shape (illustrative, adapt minimally; keep fields necessary only):\nformat: engine-lab-handoff-draft/0; status; handoff_id; release{role,platform,transport{kind: docker-archive, artifact, sha256, bytes}, expected_image_config_id, build_record, executable_sha256}; inputs{model{repository,revision,manifest,manifest_sha256}, workload{artifact,sha256}}; invocation{argv, mounts[{input|role, access}]}; sandbox_requirements{os,gpu{vendor,count},required_runtime_compatibility,network_after_staging,isolation_and_provisioning_owner: lab-team,resource_limits}; tests{requested[], policy_reference, profiling{requested,tool_and_version}}; evidence{control_and_durable_storage_outside_test_sandbox: required, outputs[], crash_outcome: interrupted-attempt-with-partial-coverage, resume: new-attempt-after-confirmed-stop}; unresolved[].\nConstraints: no network, no Docker, stdlib+PyYAML only. Do not invent a service. Time limit 40 min. Final message: files written, tests run + results, open issues.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
